  "method": {
    "poses": "Each production rig was fixed-stepped to neutral, walking, running and rolling. All cranial, dental and facial muscle triangles were compared to the actual rendered Face triangles by a separating-axis triangle test. An independent enclosure check intersected skin on either side of each head-local vertex.",
    "eyesAndHair": "Triangulated corneas, lids/lashes, and active groom pieces were transformed to the same head frame as the skull. Orbital dimensions are measured on the front inner rim. The visible frontal hairline is the first visible hair surface ahead of the actual facial skin, sampled at 0.0004 head-local units.",
    "exterior": "Orthographic depth/part-ID rasters of the original production facial surfaces and the revised Axon surfaces, nine directions including front, rear, both profiles, overhead and underside, 512 by 512 per image. This verifies silhouette and visible part identity, not GPU color equality.",
    "webglExterior": "Chromium 155 WebGL2 High and Mobile, original production hair against root-fitted hair in the same frozen Axon study, skin/hair isolated. Counts compare actual RGB readbacks from the 2D presenter after the shared WebGL renderer. Front, profile, rear and high-front views were captured at 342,370 pixels each.",
